title: The Discipline Question
subtitle: Calm the factions while remembering that unions are not under the party whip.
new-page: true
is-card: true
tags: poland_party_card
frequency: 120
view-if: month_actions < max_month_actions and poland_party_discipline_timer <= 0 and (internal_dissent >= 22 or barons_dissent >= 12 or spring_dissent >= 12 or labor_dissent >= 12 or progressives_dissent >= 12 or razem_dissent >= 12 or social_patriot_dissent >= 12)
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; poland_party_discipline_timer = 3
card-image: img/poland/cards/party-affairs.webp

= The Discipline Question

The party is no longer only a machine for winning votes. It is also a field of
competing moods. The leadership can tighten its own line or open the room.
OPZZ and the wider union movement cannot be disciplined; they can only be met
with reforms, concessions or an increasingly hostile relationship.

- @discipline
- @free_speech
- @concede_barons
- @concede_spring
- @concede_labor
- @concede_progressives
- @concede_razem
- @concede_social_patriot

@discipline
title: Enforce discipline and shut down the leak
subtitle: Party unity rises, but the most aggrieved factions feel pressed.
on-arrival: internal_dissent -= 4; party_unity += 2; barons_dissent += 2; spring_dissent += 2; labor_dissent += 2; union_trust -= 2; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; social_patriot_dissent += 2; public_trust -= 1; news_headline = "The leadership orders a tighter party line"

The whip is restored. Meetings become calmer, speeches become less frank, and
some members decide they are being managed rather than represented. Union
organisers resent being treated as though the parliamentary whip reaches them.

- #poland_card_finish

@free_speech
title: Permit free speech for a month
subtitle: Dissent falls, but the party becomes less coherent.
on-arrival: internal_dissent -= 6; party_unity -= 2; barons_dissent -= 3; spring_dissent -= 3; progressives_dissent -= 3; razem_dissent -= 3; social_patriot_dissent -= 3; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The party allows a noisy but useful month of argument"

The room becomes louder and less disciplined. The activists feel heard, and the
party's public mood softens even while its sense of direction fades.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_barons
view-if: barons_dissent >= 12
title: Concede to the Barons
subtitle: Ease the Barons' grievance and take their electorate with it; younger and urban voters read the price.
on-arrival: barons_dissent -= 8; rural_support += 2; pensioner_support += 2; local_network += 1; young_support -= 2; urban_progressive_support -= 2; progressive_credibility -= 1; spring_dissent += 3; labor_dissent += 2; union_trust -= 1; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; social_patriot_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; internal_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "The leadership placates the Barons and angers the rest"

The Barons hear a clear signal that their concerns matter. The price is that the
rest of the party sees the leadership choose a faction over the common line.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_spring
view-if: spring_dissent >= 12
title: Concede to the Spring current
subtitle: Give the Spring current room; equality voters respond and the provinces notice.
on-arrival: spring_dissent -= 8; women_support += 2; urban_progressive_support += 2; feminist_trust += 2; rural_support -= 2; pensioner_support -= 1; barons_dissent += 3; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; social_patriot_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; internal_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "Spring gets a public concession and the room hardens around it"

A compromise is offered to those who think the party is too managerial and too
slow. Other factions treat it as proof that the centre is tilting away from
them.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_labor
view-if: labor_dissent >= 12
title: Offer unions a workplace concession
subtitle: OPZZ and workplace organisers get an enforceable win; the liberal centre and party machine reprice us.
on-arrival: labor_dissent -= 8; union_trust += 5; opzz_cooperation += 5; labor_mobilization += 2; workers_support += 3; labor_credibility += 2; public_sector_support += 1; labor_reform_progress += 3; ko_relation -= 1; market_liberal_support -= 2; barons_dissent += 3; spring_dissent -= 1; progressives_dissent -= 1; razem_dissent -= 2; razem_cooperation += 1; social_patriot_dissent += 1; government_coalition_dissent += 1 if left_in_government = 1; party_unity -= 1; news_headline = "The union movement secures an enforceable workplace concession"

The concession has a clause, a deadline and named organisers capable of using
it. Razem, Wiosna and Wspólne Jutro can all claim part of the gain; the SLD
machine and liberal coalition partners must absorb the cost.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_progressives
view-if: progressives_dissent >= 12
title: Concede to the progressives
subtitle: The rights timetable gains younger voters and costs us the small-town room.
on-arrival: progressives_dissent -= 8; young_support += 3; urban_progressive_support += 2; progressive_credibility += 2; rural_support -= 2; pensioner_support -= 2; barons_dissent += 3; spring_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; social_patriot_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; internal_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "The leadership gives the progressives a public concession"

The progressives hear that equality, rights and secular governance will be part
of the party's public line. The other currents hear something like surrender.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_razem
view-if: razem_dissent >= 12
title: Concede to Razem
subtitle: The movement's activists get a signal; so do the voters we share with KO.
on-arrival: razem_dissent -= 8; young_support += 2; urban_progressive_support += 2; razem_cooperation += 3; labor_dissent -= 1; union_trust += 1; ko_relation -= 2; market_liberal_support -= 2; barons_dissent += 3; spring_dissent += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; social_patriot_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; internal_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "Razem gains an internal concession and the rest take notice"

The younger and more ambitious members hear that their concerns are not being
ignored. Everybody else hears that the party has chosen one faction's language.

- #poland_card_finish

@concede_social_patriot
view-if: social_patriot_dissent >= 12
title: Concede to the social-patriots
subtitle: The material turn reaches rural and worker voters; progressive credibility pays for it.
on-arrival: social_patriot_dissent -= 8; rural_support += 3; workers_support += 2; pensioner_support += 1; progressive_credibility -= 3; urban_progressive_support -= 2; feminist_trust -= 1; barons_dissent += 3; spring_dissent += 2; progressives_dissent += 2; razem_dissent += 2; party_unity -= 1; internal_dissent -= 2; news_headline = "The party gives the social-patriots a concession"

The party makes room for a more national and social language. Some members see
this as common sense. Others see it as a surrender to the mood that wrecks the
alliance.

- #poland_card_finish
